  "articleBody": "When installing a new shower, it's easy to make mistakes that can lead to big problems, like leaks! One of the most common issues we see is poor waterproofing. If the shower pan isn't properly sealed or the wallbacker isn't installed correctly, water can seep behind your walls, causing damage and mold. Always ensure all seams are meticulously sealed. Another frequent misstep is an incorrect drain slope or placement. If your shower floor doesn't gently slope towards the drain, water will pool, which is not only annoying but can also lead to long-term issues. Proper leveling and pitch are crucial. Don't skip flood or leak testing after the pan installation either; this step is vital to catch problems early. Finally, incorrectly sizing or positioning fixtures can cause functionality issues and just look off. A professional, like those at HH Remodeling LLC, understands these nuances and can prevent these common pitfalls. Get in touch with us at 303-505-0866 to ensure your shower is installed flawlessly.",
